# Without this file, `COPY . .` ships the host's node_modules and dist into the
# build context. That is slow, bloats the image layer cache, and — worse — the
# host's node_modules can shadow the ones installed inside the image, producing
# builds that differ from CI for reasons that are very hard to see.
node_modules
dist
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
npm-debug.log*
coverage
# `tests` is deliberately NOT excluded: the build stage runs `npm run verify`,
# which runs the suite. Excluding it made vitest exit 1 with "No test files
# found", so the image could never be gated on the tests at all.
# The runtime stage copies only `dist`, so nothing here reaches the image.
dist-smoke
# `dist-verify` is a second build made with the lab auth gate disabled, so the
# production bundle can be driven in a headless browser. It is 13 MB and must
# never enter the build context or the image.
dist-verify
*.md
!README.md
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
cloudbuild.yaml
